{"seq":16,"trial_id":"waterfall-frontier-2026-11/qm-pi-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T04:02:47.098Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"79dec85d2b31a409a14706114f5c96e5613f8a9c73ce2bebbcb1d6e726dd114d","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","text":"I found three Marrow Fieldworks ticket numbers, plus one that might be theirs.\n\n**Marrow Fieldworks tickets**\n1. **#4409**: From Moss's note \"Central handoffs next week\" (2 Jan 2026). It's a recurring timeout on the Gatehouse Check-In report at the Salina North yard (Bay 4 and the west grain-bin apron, during the 06:00 flatbed intake). Hollis flagged it before the account changed hands on 5 Jan.\n2. **#4412**: Same Moss note. It's a driver SMS prompt glitch when combine trailers are staged on unpaved overflow lots.\n3. **PD-5302**: From #central-random. Hollis posted it on Wed 14 Oct for a follow-up from this week and said no action was needed.\n\n**Might be Marrow Fieldworks**\n- **#8841**: From #central-random on Tue 13 Oct. Tobias flagged West yard Door 2 at the Plains depots double-booking when flatbeds check in early at the kiosk. Hollis called it \"Tobias's dealer account\" and didn't name the account. Moss's note says Marrow Fieldworks changed hands in January, so this may be the same account, but I can't confirm that from what I read.\n\n**Similar name, but a different account (Marrow Agrisupply)**\n- **FR-882**: A feature request in the same Moss note.\n- **PD-4821**: In #central-team on 9 Jun.\n\nMoss's other Central note (the cheat sheet) has no ticket numbers. Apart from PD-5302, nothing else from this week mentions Marrow Fieldworks: not #central-random, #central-team or our DM."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DWATERF0001","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
